<!-- Synthetic CAM (Convective Alert Modernization) severe thunderstorm
     warning, modeled on urn:oid:2.49.0.1.124.1104140223 (issue #172): one
     <info> per language, each carrying a legacy zone <area> (CLC geocode,
     large polygon) plus a freeform threat <area> (DLC geocode, small polygon
     inside the zone). Geometry is simplified to rectangles so tests can pick
     points inside/outside each ring deterministically:
       zone   ring: lat 43.0..44.0, lon -82.0..-80.0
       threat ring: lat 43.4..43.6, lon -81.2..-80.8
     The literal "issued" appears only as the DLC geocode value, so tests may
     rewrite "<value>issued</value>" to exercise the terminal tokens. -->
